  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Colombian dance-music genre of Cartagena and the Colombian Caribbean coast, emerging in 1980s from synthesis of African soukous, juju, and highlife (transmitted through cassette-and-vinyl trade with Africa via maritime sailors) with local Colombian Caribbean costeño rhythmic-vocabulary. Performed at picós large mobile sound-systems in working-class barrios. Distinguished from cumbia by champeta's African-pop-derived (vs cumbia's indigenous-Afro-Spanish-syncretic) lineage.",
